**Yes.** Apart from the choices the plan sends to Alex, I agree with v3 as amended by v4 and v5 as the plan to execute. The proposed checks still have to pass.

## 1. Round-5 disagreements

1. **Conflicting attribution — Yes, resolved as a plan.** V5 withdraws the rule that kept two conflicting records. It requires one record, a source-based attribution, both links and both summaries, followed by checks through the writer and each affected judge’s request.

   The cases are real: in [seq 1240](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1240.json:188>), the same revenue sentence names either the author or the reported data set as its original source. In [seq 1249](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1249.json:239>), the forecast’s origin differs; in [seq 1251](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1251.json:270>), the author’s estimate has an empty original day in one version and the publication day in the other. V5 requires an independent reader to check all three against their articles. That addresses the [phase PRD’s one-record rule](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:107>) and the [standard’s requirement to preserve the original speaker and meaning](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408>).

   The result is **not yet proven**: the changed request and writer-to-judge checks have not been run.

2. **Acceptance claims and comparable starting state — Yes, resolved as a plan.** V5 now says that, without a complete reference, the unseeded run reports only what readers checked; it does not claim recall or losses for the whole window. It also requires the seeded comparison to reproduce an archived control’s questions, evidence, links and judgements through the real code before sending either arm, then start the split from the identical seeded library. [Plan v5](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v5.md:22>).

   The cited [control manifest](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/r10-control-v108/d1/manifest.json>) identifies v108 and the seed file, and its [run log](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/r10-control-v108/d1/replay.log>) records the 22 seeded questions and the completed window. The archive and saved library exist. They establish that the proposed control is available; **comparability is still a gate to prove**, not an accomplished result.

## 2. New blocker or serious problem

**None found in v5.** Its proposed attribution test and archived-control replay are conditions for proceeding, not evidence that the implementation already works. In particular, reproducing the old control may fail; if it does, the plan says to stop before the comparison sends.

## 3. Agreement

**Yes**—subject to Alex’s listed decisions and the checks in the plan passing. No remaining blocker or serious disagreement with the plan itself.